  "result": "I edited three files to fix the switch-off behaviour. I did not run the test suite.\n\n- `src/server/repositories/webhook-repository.ts`: `updateEndpoint` used `...(input.enabled && { enabled })`, which dropped `false`, so switching off never saved. It now writes any explicit boolean.\n- `src/server/services/webhook-service.ts`: `createWebhook` counts every endpoint via `countEndpoints`, not only enabled ones, so switched-off endpoints keep their slot.\n- `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`: the delivery run marks a delivery failed when its endpoint is switched off as well as when it is missing.",
